Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:47:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] deps: brace-expansion 5.0.9 -> 5.0.12 (GHSA-q2hr-2g5m-vwhr,
 GHSA-qhr7-859c-m2p7, GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p)

Why a patch: this is a change to upstream's lockfile, which no
policy-pack extension can express. Upstream v0.99.1 resolves
brace-expansion 5.0.9; retire this patch at the first sync whose
upstream lockfile resolves >= 5.0.12.

What: `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high` in vendor/pi, which CI
runs, reports three denial-of-service advisories in brace-expansion
>= 4.0.0 < 5.0.12 (quadratic-time rewrite, and two unbounded
recursions on nested or comma-separated brace groups). It is a runtime
dependency, through pi-coding-agent -> minimatch 10.2.6, whose range
(^5.0.8) already admits the fix. Lockfiles only: one entry each, version,
resolved URL and integrity (checked against the registry). No manifest
changes. Two lockfiles carry it: the workspace's, and
packages/coding-agent/install-lock/package-lock.json, which upstream
generates from it for installs of the published package and which trivy
scans. The second was regenerated with `npm run
install-lock:coding-agent` and then trimmed to the brace-expansion
entry; the generator also carries 0001's pi -> gah bin rename across,
which is 0001's concern, not this patch's.

Made with `npm update brace-expansion --package-lock-only
--ignore-scripts`; audit reports 0 vulnerabilities after it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WHU6GR6xxBMmQZUcB1KhgK
